# fixtures/lq/cases/errors-text.cases: error, warning and notice goldens of [LQ/errors] (WP-22, R-FIX).
# Part 1: located errors ([LQ/errors §3.2]) for inputs that need no store: the exact text (each line ended by LF)
# and, for codes other than E001, the JSON error envelope ([LQ/errors §4.1]). The transport names the source
# (<argv>, <stdin>, <query>, or a file's base name). Spans marked 'conv' in a note follow INDEX.md §4 G-7.
# JSON goldens assume the caller's branch and tip are resolved before the text is parsed (INDEX.md §4 G-2):
# '%% context branch main' and '%% context rev 4480' give them.
# Part 2: unlocated error texts and warning and notice texts for a stated situation (the notes give the values
# the templates of [LQ/errors §5] are filled with). A renderer test builds the situation and compares the text.
# Only templates whose every placeholder has a fixed rendering are goldened here; the others are gaps G-8 and G-9.
# Format: fixtures/lq/INDEX.md §2.

%% case e005-argv
%% source [LQ/errors §3.2], §5.2 E005
%% entry read
%% transport argv
%% context branch main
%% context rev 4480
%% input
MATCH (t) RETURN t;
%% error E005 1:19 spec
%% text
error[E005 one_statement]: one statement per call; a second statement starts here
 --> <argv>:1:19
  |
1 | MATCH (t) RETURN t;
  |                   ^
  = help: send each statement in its own call, or put writes in one TX { ... } block
%% json
{"v":1,"branch":"main","rev":4480,"errors":[{"code":"E005","name":"one_statement","severity":"error","span":{"start":18,"end":19,"line":1,"col":19},"message":"one statement per call; a second statement starts here","suggest":[],"expected":[],"help":"send each statement in its own call, or put writes in one TX { ... } block","detail":[]}],"exit":2}
%% end

